806/000181080626000006/0001810806-26-000006-index.htm"},{"date":"2026-02-10","form":"8-K","codes":["5.02","7.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Director or officer departure or appointment","kind":"people","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Regulation FD disclosure","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000181080626000004/0001810806-26-000004-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-11-12","form":"8-K","codes":["5.02","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Director or officer departure or appointment","kind":"people","tone":"warn"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000119312525277998/0001193125-25-277998-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-11-05","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000181080625000167/0001810806-25-000167-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[{"date":"2020-09-29","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000119312520256885/0001193125-20-256885-index.htm","tone":"warn"}],"summary":{"sentences":["Unity Software Inc. files with the SEC under \"Services-Prepackaged Software\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 5 years.","It reported $1.9bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 16.8% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 30.8%.","Listed on NYSE, it funds itself from operations ($71.8m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 16.8% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $508.2m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000181080626000032/0001810806-26-000032-index.htm","accession":"0001810806-26-000032"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $71.8m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000181080626000032/0001810806-26-000032-index.htm","accession":"0001810806-26-000032"},{"text":"Net cash of $2.2bn against total assets of $6.5bn - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000181080626000032/0001810806-26-000032-index.htm","accession":"0001810806-26-000032"}],"bear":[{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 73.8% to 30.8% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000181080626000032/0001810806-26-000032-index.htm","accession":"0001810806-26-000032"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-69.1% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000181080626000032/0001810806-26-000032-index.htm","accession":"0001810806-26-000032"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $223.5m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000181080626000032/0001810806-26-000032-index.htm","accession":"0001810806-26-000032"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 5.4% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000181080626000032/0001810806-26-000032-index.htm","accession":"0001810806-26-000032"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 4.8% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (198,321 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000214441826000003/0002144418-26-000003-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.9% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810806/000214441826000003/0002144418-26-000003-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 23.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.23,"consecutive":2,"current":0.308,"current_display":"30.8%","threshold_display":"23.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 2.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.02,"consecutive":2,"current":0.168,"current_display":"16.8%","threshold_display":"2.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 12.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.12,"consecutive":1,"current":0.054,"current_display":"5.4%","threshold_display":"12.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.0,"current_display":"0.00","thre